1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,600
This Apollo-era mirror still works.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,200
Scientists send laser pulses from Earth.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,700
A reflector sends the light back.

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,900
The round trip takes about 2.5 seconds.

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:16,000
The signal is incredibly faint.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,800
In one NASA test, about 200 photons returned.

7
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:25,800
Timing the light measures distance to millimeters.

8
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,000
A tiny mirror. An astonishing measurement.
